/*
 * physics_objects — pushable physics objects for Hamsterball Physicus
 * (Tier 1: axis-aligned sliding/falling boxes, native ball-vs-box collision)
 *
 * RodentRacer spec (2026-08-25):
 *   - S1 ref points named  CUBE:<meshname>  spawn a physics object whose
 *     visuals AND collision come from <meshname>.MESH (MeshNode pipeline:
 *     LoadMesh 0x471750 -> MeshWorld_ctor -> MeshWorld_Parse ASE text)
 *   - No AI, no death, no respawn. Objects are NOT balls.
 *   - Ball can stand on / jump on / push the object with real mass-feel
 *   - Objects are event-inert (can't trigger N:/E: events) and immortal
 *
 * ── How it works (all Ghidra-verified) ──────────────────────────────────
 *
 *  VISUALS + COLLISION DATA: one .MESH load gives us a MeshWorld whose
 *  MeshBuffers hold strip lists (embedded AthenaList at MB+0xC: count+0x10,
 *  items+0x418, verts 32B stride, XYZ at +0/+4/+8). The game's own raycast
 *  (Mesh_FindClosestCollision 0x465D90) reads exactly these structures, so we
 *  get true mesh-vs-ball queries for free. We render manually via
 *  SceneObject_Render (vtable[18] = 0x470150, __thiscall(ECX), RET 4,
 *  arg=0 safe per waterwheel pattern).
 *
 *  PER-FRAME PHYSICS (mod-side point-mass state per object):
 *    gravity -> velocity; ground snap via downward FindClosestCollision;
 *    friction decay when grounded; integration.
 *
 *  PUSHING: if the player ball's expanded AABB overlaps the box AABB and the
 *  ball is beside it (not above), the box is pushed along the dominant X/Z
 *  approach axis. Ball keeps its own velocity (native response vs the static
 *  triangles); the box gains matching velocity -> weighty feel.
 *
 *  CARRYING: ball standing on top gets the same delta applied per frame
 *  (carry_balls pattern from lava_rising).
 *
 *  COLLISION MOVEMENT: each frame the object moves by delta D = pos - lastpos;
 *  we translate every stored ORIGINAL strip vertex by D in place. The ball's
 *  sweep query then sees the box at its new position natively. (Catapult
 *  arm-rotation technique, translation instead of rotation.)
 *
 *  RENDER MOVEMENT: MeshWorld world matrix at MW+0x04 (16 floats). We write
 *  a translation matrix each frame before calling vtable[18].
 *
 *  EVENT INERTNESS: objects are not in the ball list, so DispatchCollision-
 *  Events never sees them. No hook needed for v1.
 */

#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#include <windows.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <math.h>

typedef unsigned __int64 QWORD;

